1.Write an INNER JOIN query to fetch the order_id, customer_name, and product_name for all orders placed on your favorite food delivery app (imagine Swiggy or Zomato) using tables: Orders, Customers, and Products.
Answer :

Steps :

SELECT order_id, customer_name, product_name
FROM Orders
INNER JOIN Customers
ON Orders.customer_id = Customers.customer_id
INNER JOIN Products
ON Orders.product_id = Products.product_id;




2.Write a LEFT JOIN query to list all users from a Flipkart-style Users table and show their last order date from the Orders table, including users who have never placed an order.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Check for NULL values in the order date to identify users with no orders.</em>
Answer :

Steps :

SELECT Users.username, Orders.order_date
FROM Users
LEFT JOIN Orders
ON Users.user_id = Orders.user_id;

- The order date will be NULL for those users who has never placed order.



3.Write a RIGHT JOIN query to display all products from a Myntra-style Products table and the name of the user who last bought each product from the Users table, including products that have never been purchased.
Answer :

Steps :

SELECT Products.product_name, Users.username
FROM Users
RIGHT JOIN Products
ON Users.user_id = Products.user_id;

- This will display all the products including the products which has not been purchased. For un-purchased products the username will be NULL.




4.Write a FULL JOIN query to combine all payment transactions from a Paytm Payments table and all refund records from a Refunds table, showing transaction_id, amount, and whether it's a payment, refund, or both.
Answer :

Steps:

SELECT *
FROM Payments
FULL JOIN Refunds
ON Payments.transaction_id = Refunds.transaction_id;




5.Write a SELF JOIN query on a BookMyShow-style Movies table to find all pairs of movies that share the same genre but have different movie_ids.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Do not show pairs where both movies are the same.</em>
Answer :

Steps :

SELECT m1.movie_id, m2.movie_id, m1.genre
FROM Movies m1
JOIN Movies m2
ON m1.genre = m2.genre
AND m1.movie_id < m2.movie_id;
